From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ncrypt, crypt32, bcrypt: the software key storage provider: kept keys, decryption, ECDH, providers

ncrypt was a shell: keys could not be kept (a name was ignored with a
FIXME), NCryptOpenKey, NCryptDeleteKey, NCryptDecrypt, NCryptEnumKeys,
NCryptEnumAlgorithms, NCryptFreeBuffer and NCryptIsKeyHandle were stubs,
only RSA keys could be made, and NCryptSecretAgreement, NCryptDeriveKey and
NCryptEnumStorageProviders were "@ stub" exports. It is now the Microsoft
Software Key Storage Provider, as documented:

- Keys of RSA, DSA, DH, ECDSA_P256/P384, ECDH_P256/P384 (or ECDSA/ECDH
  with their curve set, NCRYPT_ECC_CURVE_NAME_PROPERTY), AES and 3DES are
  made by NCryptCreatePersistedKey and NCryptFinalizeKey, which makes the
  key of the length set; operations before then answer
  NTE_BAD_KEY_STATE, a second finalize NTE_INVALID_HANDLE.
- A named key is kept: for the user under %APPDATA%\Microsoft\Crypto\Keys,
  for the machine (NCRYPT_MACHINE_KEY_FLAG) under
  %ALLUSERSPROFILE%\Microsoft\Crypto\Keys, in a file named by its unique
  name, its private part protected with DPAPI. A name taken answers
  NTE_EXISTS unless NCRYPT_OVERWRITE_KEY_FLAG. NCryptOpenKey opens it
  again (NTE_BAD_KEYSET when there is none), NCryptDeleteKey removes it,
  NCryptEnumKeys lists them (NTE_NO_MORE_ITEMS at the end). Its name,
  unique name and last modified time are properties. NCryptImportKey keeps
  an imported key under the name of an NCRYPTBUFFER_PKCS_KEY_NAME
  parameter (at once, or at NCryptFinalizeKey with
  NCRYPT_DO_NOT_FINALIZE_FLAG); ECC, DH and AES blobs are taken too.
- NCryptDecrypt, and padding-less RSA's sizes; a private key leaves by
  NCryptExportKey only if its export policy allows plaintext export
  (NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED otherwise); key usage is enforced for signing,
  decryption and agreement.
- NCryptSecretAgreement and NCryptDeriveKey (ECDH, DH).
- NCryptEnumAlgorithms, NCryptEnumStorageProviders, NCryptFreeBuffer,
  NCryptIsKeyHandle (handles are checked: a handle not given out is
  NTE_INVALID_HANDLE); the provider's name, implementation type, version
  and name length; properties a software key has no value for answer
  NTE_NOT_FOUND or NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED as Windows does, and the name and
  unknown properties cannot be set (NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED).
- The platform (TPM), smart card and Passport providers answer
  NTE_DEVICE_NOT_FOUND; NCryptSignHash takes NCRYPT_SILENT_FLAG (the
  software provider never prompts); NCryptVerifySignature checks the hash
  length against the padding's algorithm and the signature against the
  key (NTE_INVALID_PARAMETER).
- crypt32: CryptAcquireCertificatePrivateKey opens a certificate's key
  kept by a CNG provider (provider type 0) as an NCrypt key when the
  caller takes one (CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ALLOW/PREFER/ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG), with
  the key spec CERT_NCRYPT_KEY_SPEC.
- bcrypt imports ECDSA_P384 private blobs (the curve was missing).

ncrypt.h and wincrypt.h get the SDK's provider names, algorithm names,
flags and NCryptProviderName. Wine's ncrypt test: all 176 todos pass and
are no longer marked; bcrypt and crypt32 cert: as before. Raw RSA
(NCRYPT_NO_PADDING_FLAG) still stops at bcrypt's backend.

Gate: test/ncryptksp-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/ncryptksp-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_KEY_STORE, SG_MUTANT_NO_DECRYPT,
SG_MUTANT_EXPORT_ANYTHING (ncrypt/main.c).
